as/pennsylvania/washington-county"],["ARC or PLC in Washington County","/arc-plc/pennsylvania/washington-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 12 grids has a record back to 1951, and September to October came in under 90% of normal in 37 of 75 years, more than any other pair. In 2025 the middle ran 46% of normal in August to September and 62% in July to August. So far in 2026, January to February came in at 51% of normal on the middle, and March to April at 137%. Grid 24198 had its driest year in 1963 at 70% of normal.</p>"}
